  "notes": "Relaxed, soul-inflected midtempo country — \"the loosest pocket in the 2000s radio cohort.\" The entry gives an explicit engine instruction and it is the model's whole identity: \"2&4 played *behind* the grid — the identity is a laid-back backbeat with the snare marginally late and low velocities; hats in lazy 8ths with ghosted 16ths; kick on 1 and 'and-of-3.' Model deliberate negative timing offset on the snare.\" That is `snare.offGridMs` at 9 with the lowest velocity tiers and the highest hat ghost share in this batch, plus a 3& secondary kick anchor. The bass is R&B-derived: \"anticipated downbeats and short rests — mixed round and forward,\" so root-following drops and anticipation goes high. Harmony is the stated \"I–IV–V with I–vi–IV–V doo-wop turns and a IV–I plagal loop on the laid-back cuts.\" Melody is \"mid-register, blues-inflected with flat-3 and flat-7 passing notes, back-phrased entries and long rests,\" which is the major_blues weighting, the raised half-step dissonance and a real `emptyBarBias`. ⚠ Confidence is medium, matching the research; the per-track readings are [LOW-CONF]. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the 9 ms snare offset itself, the velocity tiers and the counter ratio — the research says \"marginally late\" and \"low velocities\" without numbers.",
